---
// The tab convention, stated once, on every page that has tabs.
//
// Replaces the per-page paragraphs that explained the same thing in slightly
// different words — and fixes the review finding that steps referenced Kai
// without ever saying upfront what the tabs are or what Kai will ask of you.
//
// This is the "combined UI + API format" agreed on 5 August, and the same
// mechanism Michal asked for independently on 2 September ("Mám tam nějaký
// prompt? Jak to zpracuje to CLI?"). Prompt first, by construction.
//
// Plan mode, checked live 2026-09-08 (two staged runs in project 264): it adds ONE approval of
// the written plan and then asks for every change exactly as before — 8 approvals to the
// control run's 7. So it is offered here as a review gate, not as a way to approve once.
//
// Usage:  <PathIntro />                       — the default: Kai asks for approvals
//         <PathIntro approvals={false} />     — read-only pages, where it does not
//         <PathIntro yours="the Google consent screen" />
---

<div class="gs-pathintro">
  {
    Astro.props.manual === false ? (
      <p>
        <strong>This page is a prompt.</strong> The <strong>Do it with Kai</strong> tab describes
        what you want and Kai builds it. There is no click-by-click equivalent here — building
        this by hand is a development workflow with its own section, and the second tab says
        where to go for it.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        <strong>Two ways to do this, one page.</strong> The <strong>Do it with Kai</strong> tab
        is a prompt you paste; the <strong>Do it yourself</strong> tab is the same task
        click by click, for when you want to see where each setting lives. Either
        tab reaches the same result — pick one and carry on.
      </p>
    )
  }

  {
    Astro.props.approvals !== false && (
      <p>
        Kai asks before it changes anything: expect one approval dialog per
        object it creates, showing the exact configuration it is about to write.
        Questions that only read do not ask. If confirming each one gets
        tiring, pre-approve tools in{' '}
        <a href="/kai/settings/#tool-permissions">tool permissions</a>. The chat's{' '}
        <strong>plan mode</strong> button is a different thing: Kai writes the steps down
        and asks you to approve the plan before it starts — and then still asks for each
        change. Use it when you want to read the plan first, not to save clicks.
      </p>
    )
  }

  {
    Astro.props.yours && (
      <p>
        One thing stays yours either way: {Astro.props.yours}.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <p class="gs-pathintro__recovery">
    If Kai builds something other than what the page describes, say so in the
    same chat — it edits what it made. Nothing here is one-way.
  </p>
</div>
